<odoo>

    <!--
        THE group the three zone channels are gated on.

        Why a new group at all: the gate is `ir_rule_discuss_channel_all`
        (mail/security/mail_security.xml:15-26), whose only branch for
        `channel_type == "channel"` is

            group_public_id = False  OR  group_public_id IN user.all_group_ids

        so the channel is open to exactly the holders of ONE group — and the
        product needs "portal AND internal, but not the visitor". No such group
        exists in base: `group_user`, `group_portal` and `group_public` are
        three siblings with no implication between them
        (odoo/addons/base/security/base_groups.xml:42-91), so gating on
        `group_portal` would lock internal staff out and gating on `group_user`
        would lock every resident out.

        `implied_by_ids` is what makes one group cover both: a member of
        `group_user` or of `group_portal` gets this group in
        `all_group_ids` (= `group_ids.all_implied_ids`,
        odoo/addons/base/models/res_users.py:447-449), which is the exact field
        the rule reads.

        The visitor is excluded by omission, and that is the whole security
        property: a guest session runs as `base.public_user`, whose only group
        is `base.group_public` (base_groups.xml:93-95). `group_public` does NOT
        imply this group, so `group_public_id IN user.all_group_ids` is false
        for every anonymous request and the record rule filters the zone
        channels out of the `search()` that every public discuss route starts
        with. The visitor gets 404, not an empty channel.

        Note this is a READ gate, not a seat: membership plays no part in the
        rule for `channel_type == "channel"`, so seating a guest would not open
        a zone channel either. Membership is only what puts a channel in
        somebody's Discuss sidebar.
    -->
    <record id="group_zone_channel_member" model="res.groups">
        <field name="name">Community Chat: Registered Member</field>
        <field name="comment">Holders may read and post in the neighbourhood
            channels. Granted automatically to every portal and internal user;
            never granted to anonymous visitors.</field>
        <field
            name="implied_by_ids"
            eval="[Command.link(ref('base.group_user')), Command.link(ref('base.group_portal'))]"
        />
    </record>

</odoo>
